00:45:09.670 --> 00:45:22.920
"Our private reel tonight was shot in mid-air,"

00:45:22.920 --> 00:45:24.740
as we joined "Men at Work"

00:45:24.740 --> 00:45:27.530
on the northeastern leg of their U.S. tour.

00:45:27.530 --> 00:45:30.000
We spoke with lead singer Colin Haye,

00:45:30.000 --> 00:45:32.560
about music video.

00:45:32.560 --> 00:45:38.230
I think that videos play a huge part in breaking in a big way across America,

00:45:38.230 --> 00:45:41.410
especially amongst kids who see the video.

00:45:41.410 --> 00:45:45.330
It gives them more of an idea, it gives the band more of an identity,

00:45:45.330 --> 00:45:47.770
it gives them more of an idea of who that band is,

00:45:47.770 --> 00:45:52.520
and not just this other band that look like everybody else.

00:45:52.520 --> 00:45:54.720
If a band's personality and character comes across,

00:45:54.720 --> 00:45:56.750
they're ultimately much stronger.

00:45:56.750 --> 00:45:59.920
Can it be knocking at my door?

00:46:04.600 --> 00:46:08.830
Well, the humor thing isn't really something we work on, it's just there.

00:46:08.830 --> 00:46:13.880
It's not like, okay, let's have a funny clip, it's just basically that no one in the band is that serious.

00:46:13.880 --> 00:46:16.880
And their sense of humor come out.

00:46:21.160 --> 00:46:27.340
When we write a song, you don't think, well, we're going to someday make a video of this,

00:46:27.340 --> 00:46:30.000
but it just so happens that the songs...

00:46:31.340 --> 00:46:34.600
have a lot of visual elements in them, so that when you do actually come to do a video

00:46:34.600 --> 00:46:40.010
of them, it's made relatively easy, because the images are already there, and when we

00:46:40.010 --> 00:46:42.890
get together and script them, there's always an abundance of ideas.

00:46:51.310 --> 00:46:56.350
A lot of bands in America treat themselves very much as, well, I'm a rock and roll band,

00:46:56.470 --> 00:47:00.000
and this is what I do, like, my area of performance.

00:47:00.090 --> 00:47:05.860
playing the guitar on a stage but it's nowadays especially in england and australia it's it's

00:47:05.860 --> 00:47:12.100
gone way beyond that where people are actually taking other areas of performance into into

00:47:12.100 --> 00:47:17.140
account when they present themselves to the public in whatever form whether it's a live form whether

00:47:17.140 --> 00:47:23.580
it's a video form if we do a clip of performing it's just another area of performance playing on

00:47:23.580 --> 00:47:29.760
a stage isn't just that's just not what performing is to me

00:47:40.620 --> 00:47:45.070
I don't think it's the case that before us people were just standing playing guitars.

00:47:45.070 --> 00:47:47.030
I think that's largely the case with American bands.

00:47:47.030 --> 00:47:48.030
I think they still do that.

00:47:48.030 --> 00:47:51.270
I don't think many American bands have a clue how to make an interesting video.

00:47:51.270 --> 00:47:59.540
That's just my opinion, but there's a lot of bands that have been doing, really, arty clips for a long time.

00:48:00.570 --> 00:48:04.870
some bands maybe because of the fact that they've got no money they may just do a clip

00:48:04.870 --> 00:48:07.970
where they're just standing there playing guitars because they can do it for $500 or

00:48:07.970 --> 00:48:13.570
something like that but I think that American film video there is a great outlet for it but

00:48:13.570 --> 00:48:30.000
the quality isn't as good as the technology I think the clips make you much more accessible to the fans and also make

00:48:30.000 --> 00:48:35.080
them respond a lot more just in terms of when they come to shows they they wear

00:48:35.080 --> 00:48:39.160
things or they bring things to shows that they've seen in the film clips and

00:48:39.160 --> 00:48:42.380
all that sort of thing it's a it's fun it's something it's something extra

00:48:42.380 --> 00:48:46.570
something for them to get involved

00:49:00.280 --> 00:49:04.990
I don't know whether video has changed rock and roll

00:49:04.990 --> 00:49:06.280
because I've never really...

00:49:06.280 --> 00:49:09.370
I've always seen rock and roll as being a very visual thing anyway.

00:49:09.950 --> 00:49:12.540
I've never isolated rock and roll from video.

00:49:12.740 --> 00:49:16.400
I mean, I've always been part of this one big thing.

